  "title": "Native creation sees a signing's switching class between glue lines and its placement through the atoms",
  "subject": "Whether the native creation map of a plain space depends on the glue's signing only through its switching class",
  "conclusion": "For five trisum glues, each with two placements of its atoms in one switching class, removing a glue line and gluing at a glue line gives the same native vectors in both placements, while removing a line of an atom creates differently at glue lines, so the whole native maps are never isomorphic. TRISUM-READ's frozen statements hold on all five alternative placements.",
